## Data Notes

**Accounting convention flagged:** All headline IGAAP figures above reflect the **"with 1/n" IRDAI-mandated accounting convention** (effective October 1, 2024), which is the primary basis used in the presentation's headline KPI table. This is why FY25 Combined Ratio (**101.2%**) and Claims Ratio (**61.2%**) appear elevated relative to the "without 1/n" comparable figures disclosed separately (Combined Ratio **96.1%**, Claims Ratio **58.2%**). The two bases are not directly comparable, and figures for Net Worth, AUM, and Solvency Ratio follow the same "with 1/n" reporting standard for consistency.

**Two line items not disclosed** (omitted from the table above per the no-estimate rule):
- **Overall health market share** — only Retail Health market share (9.4%) is published; economy-wide health market share is not disclosed.
- **IFRS Expense ratio** — the presentation discloses only the Combined Insurance Service Ratio (103.0%) and Claims Ratio on a GEP basis (63.8%) under IFRS; no standalone IFRS expense ratio is published.

**Derived figure:** Group + others GWP (**₹2,329.7 Cr**) is calculated as Total GWP minus Retail Health GWP, since the presentation does not explicitly break out this line item — both underlying components (Total GWP and Retail Health GWP) are independently disclosed and internally consistent.

**Cross-check on PAT bridge:** IGAAP PAT (**₹213.5 Cr**, +161% YoY) reconciles to IFRS PAT (**₹203.3 Cr**, +91% YoY) via the following adjustments: Insurance Contracts (IFRS-17) +₹80.8 Cr; Income Taxes (IAS-12) −₹72.8 Cr; Share-based Payment (IFRS-02) −₹13.7 Cr; Leases (IFRS-16) −₹2.0 Cr; Financial Instruments (IFRS-09) −₹4.0 Cr; Employee Benefits (IAS-19) +₹1.4 Cr. This bridge sums correctly, confirming internal consistency of the disclosed figures.</ans>
